Microbiology — Parker and colleagues, OpenStax (@cm-microbiology-source: 0, is #reference, #part-of @cm-sources) { r_4K6CQQBY6AWTZCD0EJ5PRFGFTW
Nina Parker, Mark Schneegurt, Anh-Hue Thi Tu, Philip Lister and Brian M. Forster. *Microbiology*, OpenStax, first published 1 November 2016. [Book and downloads](https://openstax.org/details/books/microbiology) · [Preface and scope](https://openstax.org/books/microbiology/pages/preface) · [Begin reading](https://openstax.org/books/microbiology/pages/1-introduction).

Read chapters 1–3 for organisms, observation and cells; then chapters 7–9 for biochemistry, metabolism and growth, and chapter 13 for control. Use chapters 4–6 to distinguish microbial groups. The complete book offers a broader biological and medical continuation; its clinical survey is not required to understand every clean manufacturing process.

Preface, chapter outlines and selected growth/control passages were inspected on 30 October 2026, not the entire book. The current website states CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 with additional reuse notices; a free account may be requested. Do not infer the licence of a particular older PDF from the current website, or vice versa. Preserve version-specific terms and component credits. This Record links reading and does not reproduce textbook text or images.

